  "notes": "New page (coverage pass, 2026-11-08). The feature is a single grammar addition ('*' in <highlight-name-selector>) plus its zero-specificity rule; both are quoted from css-pseudo-4 §3.1. The local verification Chrome (153) predates the feature, so only the fallback path was exercised in a browser: the ::highlight(*) rule was dropped at parse and CSS.supports('selector(::highlight(*))') returned false. Chrome 158 positive behaviour (matching, specificity) is documented from the spec and ChromeStatus only, not browser-verified here. BCD has no '*' sub-feature yet, so the compat column for '*' is ChromeStatus interim data, labelled as such."
